            <ArticleTitle>Acute abdomen due to gastric volvulus: diagnostic value of a single plain radiograph.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S240</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 2(1)/2-year-old child was admitted to hospital with acute abdominal pain and vomiting. A single large air-fluid level without additional bowel gas was seen on plain abdominal radiography. At laparotomy organoaxial volvulus of the stomach was found and partial gastric resection performed. A single bubble appearance may indicate gastric volvulus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
